# WORKMITRA ENTERPRISE V2 — MANDATORY CODING & SECURITY RULES

## 1. ARCHITECTURAL INTEGRITY (6-LAYER DEFENSE)
- Always apply Zod runtime schema validation and text sanitization (sanitizeText / sanitizeUserText) on all incoming API request bodies, parameters, and drafts.
- All database write/update operations must use `withResilientTransaction` to guarantee deadlock retries (40P01) and connection pooling limits.

## 2. IDENTITY & TRANSACTION BINDING
- Never accept or trust `wm_id` or user IDs from the request body directly. Always bind to the authenticated session context (`application.worker_wm_id`).
- All shift claims and invitations must require verified tokens/proofs before state updates.

## 3. NETWORK & ENVIRONMENT HARDENING
- Ensure rate-limiting layers check sanitized IPs and session buckets.
- Never downgrade SSL settings or insert hardcoded fallback secrets. All production boots must fail hard if environment secrets (JWT_SECRET / Pepper >= 32 chars) are missing.

## 4. BUILD & TYPE STRICTNESS
- Never allow `any` types for sensitive payload fields.
- Ensure `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` pass cleanly without debug leftovers.

---

## 5. DEPLOYMENT REFERENCE (PERMANENT CONTEXT)
- Full production deployment manual (Docker, Nginx, env checklist, smoke commands): [`DEPLOYMENT.md`](./DEPLOYMENT.md)
- Before changing deploy/runtime/proxy/env behavior, read and preserve the contracts documented in `DEPLOYMENT.md`.
- Do not weaken fail-close secrets, `WM_TRUST_PROXY` + `clientIp.ts` trust rules, or Nginx `X-Forwarded-*` headers without an explicit ops decision.
